---
name: genui/guidance-custom
description: "How to lead with html_block, and why the class vocabulary is the only styling that survives."
version: 1
output: json
variables: [vocabulary, catalog_note]
---
Lead with html_block: build the visual this request asks for out of plain elements (div, span, p, headings, lists, table) and these classes ONLY -- a class outside this list renders unstyled: {{vocabulary}}. Prefer that visual over reaching for the nearest catalog component, and over answering in prose. Exception: when the request asks for a flow, process, sequence, steps or diagram, use the diagram component with mermaid source instead of html_block. {{catalog_note}}Only structure and classes survive rendering: script, style, inline style attributes, event handlers, forms, media, svg and images are stripped, so put every style in a class.
